  "about": "Where Ransom's Rest is looked at from, for screenshots and performance (Looter.Tour; Tools/tour.ps1 -Map /Game/Maps/Lvl_RansomsRest -Views Art/Levels/RansomsRest/views.json), most from the terrain's preview cameras (layout.json preview.views). x and y in cm (X north, Y east); height in cm above the first surface under the view (so never over a roof; an interior's view gives top, a world height in cm under its ceiling, where that search starts: the mine's galleries, the depot's waiting room, the watchtower's deck); yaw 0 looks north, 90 east; pitch up is positive. A view's exec runs as the tour arrives and after as it leaves: the _NoBeyond views measure what lies past the boundary (tagged Beyond) by the difference, and the _Dusk ones the level at dusk (Looter.Light Dusk behind its fade, back to Day after; on the deck the Gravewind's wisps and the canyon's fog show then). WhitlockFields is the plan's view 12: from the fields path by Amos's gate over the hay to the Whitlock barn and the windmill (Amos leans there only in a session past Main 4). DeckFight_Dusk is the plan's view 13, last because it moves the player: Abel's fight on the deck at dusk with ten adds hunting the player, who can't be hurt (Looter.Abel.Perf 10), started over as it leaves (Looter.Abel.Reset). BargeDeck_Landfall and its _Stay come after it, last because they leave the world in Main 6's state: the barge at her berth over the town with the Lamplighter grappled and the player on her well deck (Looter.Landfall 4, Looter.Barge.Show 3 aboard, Looter.Pilot.State Grappled); the camera stands where the player's eyes were (2026-11-04), at a world height: a top under the world makes the ground search find nothing, so the height is the camera's z. The far-cascade views (_FarShadow) went on 2026-11-04: they measured a far cascade the user turned down on 2026-10-07.",
